treeView-beta
  accTitle: toryo-loop files
  accDescr: The skill in shuji-skills holds the master's loop in SKILL.md, the details in references, the templates the setup copies in assets, examples in samples and the test cases in evals; each repo that uses it keeps its own setup file and agent definitions.
shuji-skills/skills/toryo-loop/
├── SKILL.md :::highlight ## the master's loop and its modes
├── README.md ## for people, never read by the agent
├── CHANGELOG.md
├── LICENSE
├── references/
│   ├── setup.md ## first run: ask, write the setup file
│   ├── tracks.md ## A, B, C and how a ticket is classified
│   ├── review.md ## levels, proof of a bug, nits, the fix round
│   ├── landing.md ## merge, check it landed, clean up
│   ├── trackers.md ## queue table, deferred, nits, the mirror
│   ├── recovery.md ## limits, a stalled agent, a false land
│   ├── claude-code.md ## agent files, models, effort, resume
│   └── trials.md ## changing the loop, the proved defaults
├── assets/
│   ├── toryo-loop.md ## the setup file template
│   ├── briefs/ ## executor and reviewer templates
│   ├── agents/ ## executor, executor-light, reviewer
│   └── guard-hook.py ## optional: main and worktree guard
├── samples/ ## a filled setup, briefs, a queue
├── showcase/ ## the README pictures
└── evals/
    └── evals.json ## trigger queries and decision scenarios
